Package: dragonfarm
Title: Fine-Tune Language Models with LoRA on Your Documents and Data
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R:
    person("Tejas", "Patel", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "algocrat@gmail.com")
Description: Fine-tune causal language models with LoRA (Low-Rank
    Adaptation) from R, and answer questions from your own documents.
    Documents (PDF, Word, HTML, Markdown, spreadsheets, web pages) are read
    into chunks, retrieved for each question by combined keyword and
    embedding search, and answered with cited sources; a model can then
    write training questions from them for review. Tables of prompts and
    responses work too. Training runs in a background 'Python' process
    built on Hugging Face 'transformers' and 'peft', with 4-bit loading
    (QLoRA) so a 7-billion-parameter model trains on an 8 GB GPU, and a
    'shiny' app covers the whole workflow. 'Python' dependencies are
    declared through 'reticulate' and resolved automatically on first use.
